# Allowlist, not a denylist. The image only ever needs the two trees the
# Dockerfile copies (backend/, frontend/), so everything else is excluded up
# front and cannot reach the daemon by accident.
#
# This matters because DATA_DIR defaults into the checkout: without this file,
# a downloaded extract sitting in ./data is sent to the daemon on every build,
# and start.sh / start.bat rebuild on every start.
*

!backend
!frontend

# Build and test residue inside the two allowed trees. None of it is used at
# runtime, and __pycache__ from the host carries paths and a Python ABI that
# do not match the image.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
